  "raw_text": "{\"options\": [\"Johannes Gutenberg's invention of the printing press revolutionized European society by enabling the rapid production of texts. This technological advancement facilitated widespread literacy and accelerated the dissemination of knowledge, influencing significant historical developments such as the Protestant Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.\", \"The introduction of the printing press by Gutenberg marked a pivotal shift in intellectual history. By making books more affordable and accessible, the press fostered the spread of new ideas and contributed substantially to the causes of the Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.\", \"Historical consensus attributes major societal transformations to the advent of the printing press. This innovation allowed for the swift production of written material, thereby playing a central role in the Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.\", \"Gutenberg's creation of the printing press fundamentally altered the course of European history. By enabling mass reproduction of texts, the press played a crucial part in the Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.\", \"The impact of Johannes Gutenberg's printing press on European history has been profound. This invention facilitated the spread of information, which played a key role in the Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.\"]}\n",
